  "notes": "{所持|しょじ} means to possess or carry something, typically in formal or legal contexts. It implies having something physically on one's person.\n\nCOMMON PATTERNS:\n- 〜を{所持|しょじ}する: to possess, to carry ~\n\nCOMMON COLLOCATIONS:\n- {所持|しょじ}{品|ひん}: personal belongings, items on one's person\n- {所持|しょじ}{金|きん}: money on hand, cash carried\n- {銃|じゅう}を{所持|しょじ}する: to carry a gun\n- {不法|ふほう}{所持|しょじ}: illegal possession\n\nSIMILAR WORDS:\n- {所有|しょゆう}: ownership (broader, includes property and rights)\n- {持|も}つ: to have, to hold (everyday word)",
